{"id": "EUVD-2026-59069", "enisaUuid": "3a8c1b2e-02f6-361f-84e7-e9e5d1939837", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Reset register bounds before narrowing retval range in check_mem_access()\n\nWhen the BPF verifier processes a context load of an LSM hook return\nvalue, it calls __mark_reg_s32_range() to narrow the register to the\nhook's valid range. However, __mark_reg_s32_range() intersects the new\nrange with the register's existing bounds using max_t()/min_t() rather\nthan replacing them.\n\nIf the destination register carries stale bounds from a prior instruction\n(e.g. BPF_MOV64_IMM), the intersection can produce a range narrower than\nreality. The verifier then believes it knows the register's exact value,\nwhile at runtime the actual hook return value is loaded, creating a\nverifier/runtime mismatch that can be used to bypass BPF memory safety\nchecks.\n\nThe else branch already calls mark_reg_unknown() to reset register state\nbefore any narrowing. Apply the same reset in the is_retval path so\nstale bounds are cleared before __mark_reg_s32_range() intersects.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:52:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:44:56", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bde92f65042ec14389782dd223f706bf6b59ce5d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0993dc5fc619c0b25ab1310cb11d65e78351c0fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a55f9aecc08990940e70f0c7048a80850c5a16a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e0b273e0a62cc04ec338c7b502797c66c2ed42a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72111", "GHSA-vhcf-p8jc-x5f6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00dca455-6ca5-3e3c-b23d-5e2e2ad5ec8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11.2 <6.12"}, {"id": "08ba5a7e-6363-3696-8fcb-aa3431fb7927", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5d99e198be279045e6ecefe220f5c52f8ce9bfd5 <bde92f65042ec14389782dd223f706bf6b59ce5d"}, {"id": "11bb87d8-0c79-3cda-ba84-6da160122434", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10.13 <6.11"}, {"id": "2463df28-d805-3782-9193-0d1206fbfa01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "33c21e57-dfb4-3f58-8b74-06953544e738", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "4dfed7cb-cd62-381b-9841-4ca42403b6a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "537405e0-b436-30ab-9f11-38106359c524", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5d99e198be279045e6ecefe220f5c52f8ce9bfd5 <5a55f9aecc08990940e70f0c7048a80850c5a16a"}, {"id": "6336f172-59e3-3de8-bf6d-90dc7cfd9efe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "85ca3732-8933-3573-88dd-4fc74c454e52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "8e461764-080b-3604-bc26-ac9839d2498b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.103"}, {"id": "946c49e3-3798-360e-94e9-09adc76484c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5d99e198be279045e6ecefe220f5c52f8ce9bfd5 <5e0b273e0a62cc04ec338c7b502797c66c2ed42a"}, {"id": "9836f53c-9132-3cb0-a076-a4f1efa57dc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1050727d83e70449991c29dd1cf29fe936a63da3"}, {"id": "cba04939-dfa7-3283-818b-1087dc9a9e0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27ca3e20fe80be85a92b10064dfeb56cb2564b1c"}, {"id": "f20cb702-1026-34c0-801e-f750ade6621c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5d99e198b